<title>CANADA: Gunfire briefly halts Arakis drilling in Sudan.</title>
<headline>Gunfire briefly halts Arakis drilling in Sudan.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arakis Energy Corp confirmed reports on Monday of a shooting incident overnight at a southern Sudan drilling location.</p>
<p>No injuries or damage were reported.</p>
<p>&quot;There was an incident in the field,&quot; Arakis chief executive John McLeod said in an interview. &quot;We shut the rig down for a few hours and we're back drilling again this morning.&quot;</p>
<p>McLeod said responsibility for what had been reported as machine gun fire had not yet been claimed.</p>
